"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":7,\"name\":\" [0.03s]\",\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":7,\"status\":\"completed\"}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":0,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.48] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"Ontology learning is becoming a sub-area of ontology engineering due to the exponential growth of web documents and the cutting-edge techniques shared by the machine learning, natural language process- ing, information retrieval, and arti\\ufb01cial intelligence communities. Ex- isting ontologies have generally been created manually. This method of creating ontology has traditionally been used by most ontology en- gineers, even if this procedure is exceedingly error-prone and time- consuming which makes it di\\ufb03cult to maintain and update ontologies. Due of this, researchers have constantly explored new approaches to produce or maintain and update ontologies in both e\\ufb03cient and ef- fective ways [127] . This survey aims to highlight the main contribu- tions on ontology generation, providing descriptions of the most pop- ular and widely used ontology development environments (ODEs), in- cluding Prot\\u00e9g\\u00e9 [128] , Topbraid Composer [26] , Ontostudio [27] , Flu- ent Editor [28] , VocBench [29] ,\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":1,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.282] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"reference manual. 1992.\\n\\n[108] Farquhar A, Fikes R, Rice J. The ontolingua server: A tool for collaborative ontology\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=12\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":2,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.229] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"equipped with the capability to shape and combine various ontologies, thus ensuring the potential of developing shared and reusable informa- tion archives. Swoop\\u2019s predisposition to integration is less clear; it fol- lows di\\ufb00erent principles. It has commands for the fusion of ontologies, but developers were mainly concerned with operations for the reuse of contents within the same ontology: the Swoop \\u201cResource Holder \\u201d tool. OBO-Edit integrations also regard contents in the same ontology. On- toStudio allows the development and maintenance of ontologies by us- ing graphical means, based on client/server architecture. In OntoStudio the ontologies are managed in a central server and users can access and redesign the ontologies. TopBraid Composer (FE) may use in a single user mode working with ontologies stored as \\ufb01les or in a database.\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=8\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":3,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.52] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[Image of the page 4]\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":4,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.230] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"3.8.5. Documentation\\n\\nThe Prot\\u00e9g\\u00e9 user manual is relatively straightforward; it contains an introduction that explains all theoretical and conceptual aspects of ontologies and languages for the semantic web. This site has produced good, comprehensive updated work, becoming thus a great resource for all Prot\\u00e9g\\u00e9 users. Swoop, OntoStudio and TopBraid Composer (FE) ed- itors provide documentation ontology and ontology libraries. A user\\u2019s guide to the program is provided by Fluent Editor, VonBench and OBO- Edit. The huge and well-organized materials are made possible by frame- works with hypertext links.\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=8\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":5,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.44] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[Image of the page 4]\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":6,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.63] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"OntoStudio 3.2.0 [27] has been the widely used and accepted tool for building and maintaining ontologies a few years ago [106] . Its prede- cessor version was called OntoEdit [131] . It is a multilingual editor and ontology modeler with a lot of customization options. French, English and German are the languages that can de\\ufb01ne synonyms. Classes, prop- erties, rules, queries and mapping are all part of it. This editor supports the OWL, RDF and ObjectLogic formats [27] . When starting a project, users have the option to choose their preferred storage type, includ- ing internal repositories or a collaborative server. Di\\ufb00erent \\ufb01le formats, such as xml, html, doc, ppt, pdf and postscript, can store data. With the use of a query builder, it provides the option to get data from databases, such as a SQL database. The availability of Query Builder SQL makes it simple to design queries. An external OntoStudio support tool called On- toBroker uses ObjectLogic and SPARQL to query the graph. SPARQL\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=5\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":7,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.248] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"Declaration of Competing Interest\\n\\nThe authors declare that they have no known competing \\ufb01nancial interests or personal relationships that could have appeared to in\\ufb02uence the work reported in this paper.\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=11\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":8,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.45] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[Image of the page 4]\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":9,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.14] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"Ontologies\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=2\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":10,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.291] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[131] Cardoso J. Semantic Web Services: Theory, Tools and Applications: Theory, Tools\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=13\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":11,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.46] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[Image of the page 4]\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":12,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.245] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"Fig. 7. OntoGraph relationships.\\n\\ngeneral characteristics and common knowledge regarding experimental studies, as well as to allow the communication among users, opening the opportunity to explore e-science concepts into the LS experimenta- tion domain. Potential future research directions would be to automate the process of creating the ontology. Beyond the creation of new on- tologies, another challenging area of work in the subject of ontologies is the evolution and mapping of current ontologies. Due to the cost of cre- ation, abstraction, and reusability, this is signi\\ufb01cant. Di\\ufb00erent types of ontologies can be derived from a core ontology to suit particular appli-\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=10\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":13,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.79] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"in order to transmit entities to various ontologies. To reuse entities already present in other works, users are thus required to employ links rather than pure importations. Swoop does not currently support trading with shares, but a \\u201dsimple copy-paste \\u201d could provide a workaround.\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=6\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":14,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.47] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[Image of the page 4]\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=4\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":15,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.292] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"and Applications. IGI Global; 2007 .\\n\\n[132] Erdmann M, Waterfeld W. Overview of the neon toolkit. In: Ontology Engineering\\n\\nin a Networked World. Springer; 2012. p. 281\\u2013301 .\\n\\n[133] Singh A, Anand P. State of art in ontology development tools. Int J\\n\\n2013;2(7):96\\u2013101 .\\n\\n[134] Motik B, Studer R. Kaon2\\u2013a scalable reasoning tool for the semantic web. In: Pro- ceedings of the 2nd European Semantic Web Conference (ESWC\\u201905), 17, Heraklion, Greece; 2005 .\\n\\n[135] Arpirez JC, Corcho O, Fern\\u00b4andez-L\\u00b4opez M, G\\u00b4omez-P\\u00b4erez A. Webode in a nut-\\n\\nshell. AI Mag 2003;24(3) 37\\u201337 . [136] Top Quadrant. Topbraid composer, 2011. [137] Pollock JT. Semantic web for dummies. John Wiley and Sons; 2009 . [138] European Commission. Isa2-interoperability solutions for public administrations,\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=13\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":16,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.67] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"Fluent Editor [28] is an entirely free and open source. It o\\ufb00ers Pro- t\\u00e9g\\u00e9 interoperability by installing the necessary plug-in, allowing users to edit ontologies in natural language and working with the majority of the Semantic Web W3C standard [106] . Using the selected materializa- tion pro\\ufb01le, the user can display the ontology as an interactive diagram and immediately analyze the results. Fluent Editor gives the user access to the SWRL Debugger, a tool for creating actual ontologies and express- ing intricate conditional relationships as examples. The \\ufb01rst iteration of an embedded SWRL debugger has been made available by the develop- ers to assist users while they model with SWRL. It enables the user to see which rules were put into action during materialization and which entities were employed in place of their head clauses and body. The user will concentrate on the real meaning of the ontology being updated (e.g., taxonomy, vocabulary, rule set). Using an R language program to\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=5\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":17,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.255] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"[8] Tudorache T. Ontology engineering: Current state, challenges, and future direc-\\n\\ntions. Semant Web 2020;11(1):125\\u201338 .\\n\\n[9] Bodenreider O, Burgun A. Biomedical ontologies. In: Medical Informatics. Springer;\\n\\n2005. p. 211\\u201336 .\\n\\n[10] Poggi A, Lembo D, Calvanese D, De Giacomo G, Lenzerini M, Rosati R. Linking data to ontologies. In: Journal on data semantics X. Springer; 2008. p. 133\\u201373 . [11] Dameron O, Fridman Noy N, Knublauch H, Musen MA. Accessing and manipulating\\n\\nontologies using web services. Sws@ iswc; 2004 .\\n\\n[12] Bateman JA. On the relationship between ontology construction and natural lan- guage: a socio-semiotic view. Int J Hum Comput Stud 1995;43(5):929\\u201344 . [13] Schulze-Kremer S. Adding semantics to genome databases: towards an ontology for\",\"reference_url\":\"files/DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf#page=11\"}],\"status\":null}]}},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1759151387,\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":null}\n\ndata: {\"id\":\"2e538b8d-8520-478d-9385-449b0e42bcf7\",\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"custom_content\":{\"stages\":[{\"index\":4,\"attachments\":[{\"index\":18,\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"title\":\"[0.260] DpZGXdhaTxtaR67JyAHgDVkSP3Fo4nvV4FYCWNadE2Ln/ontologies.pdf\",\"data\":\"editing browser. J Web Semant 2006;4(2):144\\u2013